DESCRIPTION:[] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13505106/p
 review?hidden=1)\n\nEstimated time: 40 minutes\n\nWatch this video about d
 iscussion board guidelines for the semester:\n\n[Discussions Transcript] (
 https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13505320?wrap=1)\n\nYou wi
 ll have the opportunity in upcoming lessons to study many talks and messag
 es taught by President Oaks. In this unit\, you have learned more about hi
 s calling and his biography. Now we will consider this question together: 
 In what ways is his life a sermon? Follow the prompts below to share lesso
 ns you learned from his life experience.\n\nFor this discussion\, you will
  make two separate posts:\n\n* Post 1\, due by Tuesday: Write two solid pa
 ragraphs (4–6 sentences each)\n\n* Each paragraph should very briefly me
 ntion one particular life theme or event from President Oaks's life (you d
 o not need to repeat its details)\,\n\n* Then explain what principles you 
 learned\, and\n\n* Comment on how you can apply that example in your own l
 ife and circumstances.\n\n* Post 2\, due by Wednesday: After reading 5+ of
  your peers' posts\, make a separate\, one-paragraph Summary + Response po
 st. What themes and additional ideas stood out to you in the examples and 
 thoughts they shared?\n\nFull points will be rewarded for one initial post
  plus a later Summary + Response post\, with each demonstrating considered
  engagement related to the lesson material.\n\nRubric: You will earn up to
  6 points for the content and requirements of your initial post (each para
 graph: event\, principle\, application) and 4 points for your thoughtful s
 ummary and response to the group discussion. To see the complete rubric\, 
 click on the three dots in the top right corner of this page. Then click "
 Show Rubric."\n\nModule Item Completion (built in browser\, hidden in app)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://byu.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course
 _35044&month=09&year=2026#assignment_1441108
