BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Discussion: Studying Prophetic Teachings [REL C 333-033]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260919
DTSTAMP:20261005T135100Z
UID:event-assignment-1441095
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:[] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13505106/p
 review?hidden=1)\n\nEstimated time: 40 minutes\n\nAs part of your reading 
 preparation\, you were asked to pick two study methods from the list of su
 ggestions in lesson 1 (from both the text chapter and the lesson content) 
 and then apply those methods as you read two of the five assigned seminal 
 talks by President Oaks. The method you used for his most recent conferenc
 e talk will be addressed separately in the quiz.\n\nFor each talk\, write 
 a solid paragraph (approximately 4–6 sentences) about your own study exp
 erience. Include the following:\n\n* Which study method did you choose for
  each talk? (Identify both the title and the method applied.)\n\n* Name on
 e or two things you learned as you studied.\n\n* Explain how the chosen st
 udy method affected your learning experience.\n\nThen reply thoughtfully t
 o two other students’ comments.\n\nYour posts and replies are due by the
  date indicated at the top of this discussion. Full points will be awarded
  for one comment plus two replies\, with each demonstrating considered eng
 agement related to the lesson material.\n\nYou must submit your own respon
 se before you can see other students’ comments. Do not worry about being
  redundant or saying something “original.” It’s acceptable for sever
 al people to comment on similar topics from the reading\; simply share wha
 t was the most meaningful for you personally. Once your own comment is sub
 mitted\, identify two of your peers' posts to which you can reply with tho
 ughtful and genuine reflection (minimum 2-3 sentences\, see rubric).\n\nRu
 bric: You will earn up to 6 points for content and requirements of your in
 itial post and 4 points for your thoughtful replies to two other students.
  To see the complete rubric\, click on the three dots in the top right cor
 ner of this page. Then click "Show Rubric."\n\nModule Item Completion (bui
 lt in browser\, hidden in app)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://byu.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course
 _35044&month=09&year=2026#assignment_1441095
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instruct
 ure-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachments/8409020
 /dp_app.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instructure-uploads.s3.a
 mazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachments/8073295/canvas-byuonlin
 e-app.css"><p><img src="https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13
 505106/preview?hidden=1" alt="" width="2389" height="554" data-decorative=
 "true" data-api-endpoint="https://byu.instructure.com/api/v1/courses/35044
 /files/13505106" data-api-returntype="File" loading="lazy"></p>\n<p><span 
 style="font-size: 10pt\;"><em>Estimated time: 40 minutes</em></span></p>\n
 <p>As part of your reading preparation\, you were asked to pick two study 
 methods from the list of suggestions in lesson 1 (from both the text chapt
 er and the lesson content) and then apply those methods as you read two of
  the five assigned seminal talks by President Oaks. <em>The method you use
 d for his most recent conference talk will be addressed separately in the 
 quiz.</em></p>\n<p>For each talk\, write a solid paragraph (approximately 
 4–6 sentences) about your own study experience. Include the following:</
 p>\n<ul>\n<li>Which study method did you choose for each talk? (Identify b
 oth the title and the method applied.)</li>\n<li>Name one or two things yo
 u learned as you studied.</li>\n<li>Explain how the chosen study method af
 fected your learning experience.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Then reply thoughtfully t
 o two other students’ comments.</p>\n<div>Your posts <em>and</em> replie
 s are due by the date indicated at the top of this discussion. Full points
  will be awarded for one comment plus two replies\, with each demonstratin
 g considered engagement related to the lesson material.</div>\n<p>You must
  submit your own response before you can see other students’ comments. D
 o not worry about being redundant or saying something “original.” It
 ’s acceptable for several people to comment on similar topics from the r
 eading\; simply share what was the most meaningful for you personally. Onc
 e your own comment is submitted\, identify two of your peers' posts to whi
 ch you can reply with thoughtful and genuine reflection (minimum 2-3 sente
 nces\, see rubric).</p>\n<p><strong>Rubric:</strong> You will earn up to 6
  points for content and requirements of your initial post and 4 points for
  your thoughtful replies to two other students. To see the complete rubric
 \, click on the three dots in the top right corner of this page. Then clic
 k "Show Rubric."</p>\n<p class="kl_module_progress_completion" style="disp
 lay: none\;">Module Item Completion (built in browser\, hidden in app)</p>
 <script src="https://instructure-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_74070000
 000000001/attachments/8409019/dp_app.js"></script>
END:VEVENT
