SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:[] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13505106/p
 review?hidden=1)\n\nEstimated time: 2 minutes\n\nSubmit your apostle resea
 rch paper here.\n\nAs a reminder\, you should have studied the six most re
 cent general conference talks given by that individual\, looking for instr
 uctional patterns\, recurring themes\, and lessons related to his biograph
 y (the biography link is provided below).\n\n[President Dallin H. Oaks’ 
 biography] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/pages/biography-dall
 in-h-oaks)\n\n[President Jeffrey R. Holland’s biography] (https://byu.in
 structure.com/courses/35044/pages/mastercourse_7407_842_3e05e4da553cf3c311
 3fd101986d651f)\n\n[President Henry B. Eyring’s biography] (https://byu.
 instructure.com/courses/35044/pages/biography-henry-b-eyring)\n\n[Elder Di
 eter F. Uchtdorf’s biography] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044
 /pages/biography-dieter-f-uchtdorf)\n\n[Elder David A. Bednar’s biograph
 y] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/pages/biography-david-a-bedn
 ar)\n\n[Elder Quentin L. Cook’s biography] (https://byu.instructure.com/
 courses/35044/pages/biography-quentin-l-cook)\n\n[Elder D. Todd Christoffe
 rson’s biography] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/pages/biogr
 aphy-d-todd-christofferson)\n\n[Elder Neil L. Andersen’s biography] (htt
 ps://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/pages/biography-neil-l-andersen)\n
 \n[Elder Ronald A. Rasband’s biography] (https://byu.instructure.com/cou
 rses/35044/pages/biography-ronald-a-rasband)\n\n[Elder Gary E. Stevenson
 ’s biography] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/pages/biography
 -gary-e-stevenson)\n\n[Elder Dale G. Renlund’s biography] (https://byu.i
 nstructure.com/courses/35044/pages/biography-dale-g-renlund)\n\n[Elder Ger
 rit W. Gong’s biography] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/page
 s/biography-gerrit-w-gong)\n\n[Elder Ulisses Soares’ biography] (https:/
 /byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/pages/biography-ulisses-soares)\n\n[Eld
 er Patrick Kearon’s biography] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/3504
 4/pages/biography-patrick-kearon)\n\nAs a reminder\, you can check which a
 postle you signed up for here:\n\n[Make a link to your Google Doc here--se
 e Instructor Setup Notes]--then delete this]Signup Sheet Link[End Link])\n
 \nWhere possible\, these should be six of the apostle’s most recent gene
 ral conference talks\, including (if you choose) talks given in priesthood
  or women’s sessions. Also\, where possible\, these should be talks give
 n after their call to the apostleship. If six are not available\, you may 
 include talks from devotionals or other settings in which the apostle has 
 given talks prior to their call as an apostle.\n\nRequirements\n\n* The pa
 per should be 2–3 pages long\, with a word count between 750 and 1\,000 
 words. State the word count below your conclusion. The bibliography\, a ti
 tle page\, or any other addenda will not count toward the word count.\n\n*
  Submit the paper as a Word document or PDF in 12-point Times New Roman fo
 nt\, double spaced\, with one-inch margins.\n\n* Use the rubric below as a
  checklist to see if you meet all the requirements. See the [assignment de
 scription] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/pages/apostle-resear
 ch-paper-introduction) for more details. You may also review [this example
  paper] (https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GvobGQCqXo_3Kri3eWqDgTuZxiieVHql
 /view?usp=sharing) to help you.\n\nModule Item Completion (built in browse
 r\, hidden in app)
