SUMMARY:Checkpoint: Action Plan Video (F/W) [REL C 333-033]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTSTAMP:20261007T183900Z
UID:event-assignment-1441094
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:[] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13505106/p
 review?hidden=1)\n\nEstimated time: 30 minutes\n\n------------------------
 -----\nCheckpoint: Action Plan Video\n-----------------------------\n\nIn 
 this Checkpoint activity\, you will participate in a small-group video "di
 scussion" with your instructor team and several classmates about favorite 
 talks from general conference and application ideas.\n\nWatch the followin
 g video to hear some of your instructor team's conference reflections:\n\n
 https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/discussion_topics/748371\n\nYou 
 will make three posts:\n\nPost 1: Reply to the instructor/TA video with an
 y comments you have to add to the conversation about what your instructor(
 s) shared or in response to any questions posed. Simply click on reply at 
 the bottom of these instructions. This response can be written.\n\nPost 2:
  Then\, you will record a video in which you react to your favorite talk a
 nd articulate an action plan based on that talk. (It's fine if your favori
 te is the same as someone else in the discussion\; give us your take on wh
 at you learned.) Your video should include these elements:\n\n* Identify t
 he speaker and talk you want to highlight from the recent general conferen
 ce\,\n\n* Briefly share teachings that were meaningful to you personally\;
  Choose any portion of the talk you want to react to (overall themes\, a b
 rief snippet or quote\, etc.)\, but provide some kind of summary of the te
 achings and principles you learned. \n\n* Outline some specific ideas for
  application\, including a plan of action with short-term and long-term st
 eps. (You may be as detailed or general as you feel comfortable sharing.)
 \n\nYour video should only be approximately 1-2 minutes long\, but it shou
 ld clearly address the required items. You can create it in any way you se
 e fit as long as it references one of the recent general conference talks 
 and meets the content requirements listed above\; be creative\, but you ca
 n be as high-tech or low-tech as you're comfortable with.\n\nUpload/Embed 
 a video file or a link to it\; make sure any video links are shared for pu
 blic view. Here are several options and instructions for recording and sha
 ring your video: [Resources for Creating Videos] (https://byu.instructure.
 com/courses/35044/pages/resources-for-creating-videos)\n\nPost your reacti
 on video file or link onto this discussion board\, and write the name of t
 he speaker and/or name of the talk you are highlighting. I encourage you t
 o create and share your video on your own social media channels. If it's p
 ublicly viewable\, please include that link in your post here.\n\nPost 3: 
  After you post your video \, watch videos from other students in the dis
 cussion group. Reply to one or more of your peer's videos to add to the co
 nversation\; your reply can be either video or written. You may share your
  own thoughts about the talk or principles they shared or highlight connec
 tions to other general conference talks or your own experience.\n\nIn summ
 ary\, reply to the instructor video\, post your own original reaction vide
 o\, and reply to a classmate's video by the indicated due date. Once you h
 ave completed the three posts\, your Checkpoint is complete. This is a sma
 ll-group discussion\, so please participate in a timely manner as other st
 udents will be awaiting your video before they can respond.\n\nRubric: For
  your own reaction video\, you will earn up to 6 points based on the three
  requirements in the instructions. You will earn up to 2 points for your r
 eply to the instructor(s) and another 2 points for your reply to another s
 tudent's video. To see the complete rubric\, click on the three dots in th
 e top right corner of this page. Then click "Show Rubric."\n\nModule Item 
 Completion (built in browser\, hidden in app)
