BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:General Conference Reflection Assignment (F/W) [REL C 333-033]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTSTAMP:20261005T135200Z
UID:event-assignment-1441133
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:[] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13505106/p
 review?hidden=1)\n\nEstimated time: 40 minutes\n\nNote: Because this is a
  Living Prophets class\, general conference is an important highlight of o
 ur semester\; therefore\, this assignment is worth twice the value of othe
 r units’ assignments.\n\nThe content of this assignment will be your ref
 lections on the addresses from the most recent general conference of the C
 hurch.\n\nYou will answer the following questions thoughtfully\, drawing u
 pon your own experience participating in [general conference (Links to a
 n external site.)] (http://gc.churchofjesuschrist.org/)\; you may refer to
  notes or review any of the talks that are available online. Respond to ea
 ch question with a solid paragraph (minimum 3–4 sentences).\n\n* What th
 emes and repetition did you notice during this general conference?\n\n* Su
 mmarize briefly what stood out to you from President Oaks’s talks or ann
 ouncements or communications during general conference. (On an upcoming ex
 am\, you’ll be asked to analyze his general session talk more deeply.)\n
 \n* Identify a promised blessing and what you need to do to obtain it from
  President Eyring’s general session talk\, and share your main takeaway 
 from his message.\n\n* Identify a promised blessing and what you need to d
 o to obtain it from President Christofferson’s general session talk\, an
 d share your main takeaway from his message.\n\n* Choose one of the foll
 owing to answer:\n\n* Comment briefly on the talk by the apostle from your
  apostle paper. How did your preparation affect your reception of his mess
 age\, and what did you notice?\n\n* Comment on any experience you had find
 ing answers to questions or receiving what Elder Holland called “a perso
 nal prophetic epistle just to you.”[1] (#end) (You may be as specific o
 r general as you feel comfortable sharing.)\n\n* Did you watch (or listen 
 to) at least four general sessions of general conference? Yes/No: No parag
 raph is necessary. If no\, please indicate how much you completed.\n\n----
 -----------------------------\nRequirements for this assignment:\n--------
 -------------------------\n\n* title (“General Conference Reflections”
 ) and your name at the top\n\n* 2–3 pages total\n\n* 12-point Times New 
 Roman font\n\n* double spaced\n\n* one-inch margins\n\n* .doc\, .docx\, or
  .pdf format\n\nSubmission Instructions\n-----------------------\n\nWhen y
 ou are ready to upload and submit this assignment:\n\n* Click Submit Assig
 nment in the top-right corner.\n\n* Attach the relevant assignment by cli
 cking the Choose File button\, then locating the file you wish to submit
 .\n\n* When you are finished\, click Submit Assignment.\n\n* You should r
 eceive a message in the top-right corner telling you your assignment was t
 urned in.\n\nRubric: \n--------\n\nYou will earn 5 points for watching fo
 ur+ sessions of general conference and 3 points each for the content and r
 equirements of paragraphs 1–5.\n\nModule Item Completion (built in brows
 er\, hidden in app)\n\n----------\nReferences\n----------\n\n1 Jeffrey R. 
 Holland\, “[An Ensign to the Nations] (https://www.churchofjesuschrist.o
 rg/study/ensign/2011/05/sunday-afternoon-session/an-ensign-to-the-nations?
 lang=eng)\,” Ensign or Liahona\, May 2011.
