SUMMARY:Discussion: Eyring and Christofferson Sweet Spots [REL C 333-033]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTSTAMP:20261010T060000Z
UID:event-assignment-1441106
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:[] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13505106/d
 ownload?hidden=1)\n\nEstimated time: 30 minutes\n\nThis is a “sweet spot
 ” discussion where you can share some personal thoughts about any of the
  assigned readings. A sweet spot is something that had an impact on you as
  you studied\, usually where the Spirit grabbed your attention. For questi
 ons 1 and 2\, you can comment on anything that stood out to you during you
 r preparation—something you learned\, a powerful quote/principle/theme\,
  a connection you made\, or ideas about application.[] (https://byu.instru
 cture.com/users/37820/files/1389251/preview?hidden=1&verifier=LVG7tJeq1kDL
 bexqeCD5DeJnYYXqMJh1SIbd6avz)\n\n* What was your sweet spot from the biogr
 aphies of either President Eyring or President Christofferson?\n\n* What w
 as your sweet spot from any of the assigned talks by President Eyring or P
 resident Christofferson?\n\n* Share any similarities you noticed across th
 eir messages\, as well as with President Oaks’s talks you studied earlie
 r. (What do you see them teaching unitedly as a First Presidency?)\n\nAnsw
 er each question with a solid paragraph\, 4-6 sentences. Your posts and re
 plies are due by the date indicated at the top of this discussion. Full po
 ints will be rewarded for your original post plus two replies (to another 
 student's post and/or comments on your post)\, with each demonstrating con
 sidered engagement related to the lesson material.\n\nRubric: You will ear
 n up to 6 points for your initial post (2 points per question) and 4 point
 s for two replies to other students’ posts. To see the complete rubric\,
  click on the three dots in the top right corner of this page. Then click 
 "Show Rubric."\n\nModule Item Completion (built in browser\, hidden in app
 )
