DESCRIPTION:[] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13505106/d
 ownload?hidden=1)\n\nEstimated time: 20 minutes\n\n-----------------------
 ------------\nWhat to Expect from This Checkpoint\n-----------------------
 ------------\n\nThis is 1) a “sweet spot” activity and 2) a review of 
 your semester goals. A sweet spot is something that had an impact on you a
 s you studied\, usually where the Spirit grabbed your attention. You will 
 converse with your instructor or TA about what has stood out to you in you
 r study of the course material up to the point of your conference. You can
  comment on anything you are learning—a powerful quote/principle/theme\,
  a connection you made\, or ideas about application. You may have time to 
 ask the instructor any questions you have about the course.[] (https://byu
 .instructure.com/users/37820/files/1389251/preview?hidden=1&verifier=LVG7t
 Jeq1kDLbexqeCD5DeJnYYXqMJh1SIbd6avz)\n\nYou can schedule this checkpoint a
 ny time between now and the last day of classes. NOTE: This checkpoint con
 ference is a one-time assignment\; you will see multiple reminders for thi
 s checkpoint\, but you only need to attend once. (You can still use office
  hours whenever you need them for other matters as well.)\n\nPurpose\n----
 ---\n\nThe class setup doesn't often allow for one-on-one interaction with
  the instructor\, this checkpoint conference invites you to reflect on and
  talk about what you are learning in the class. Its purpose is a conversat
 ion about subject matter that is meaningful to you and worth your time to 
 talk about\, so please schedule and plan accordingly as you read the cours
 e content. It also allows your instructor team to interact with you person
 ally\, review your course goals with you\, hear about your learning experi
 ence\, and respond to questions you might have.\n\nBefore Your Checkpoint
 \n----------------------\n\nSchedule your appointment following the instru
 ctions on the [Instructor/TA Contact & Scheduling Information] (https://d
 ocs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1wGfmOFXndwp1eG-t3m_Jxs4wAZsJwWRQlt6-KVeBxQg
 /edit?usp=sharing) page\; you can sign up for a fifteen-minute appointment
  with the instructor or any of the TAs. (You can choose the time that best
  fits your schedule\, even if it’s not with the TA from your own section
 .) If you already know the posted office hours are impossible for your sc
 hedule\, reach out early to your own TA (before the close of Unit 10) and 
 you can coordinate a mutually agreeable alternate time to meet before the 
 end of the semester. Because of the end-of-semester course workload\, we w
 ill not be scheduling or creating any extra office hours during the last t
 hree units of the semester.\n\nPlanning options: Either go ahead and make 
 an appointment now for a future date\, and as it approaches\, pay careful 
 attention to what you’re studying and choose something you want to share
  and talk about\, or as you go about your regular class preparations\, if 
 something specific stands out and you’d love to discuss it\, make an app
 ointment for the near future. Either way\, come prepared to share and disc
 uss your “sweet spot(s).”\n\nDuring Your Checkpoint\n-----------------
 -----\n\nAfter brief greetings\, you will be asked to share your sweet spo
 t(s). We may ask you some follow-up questions about what you share\, and w
 e’ll also discuss the class goals you submitted in the "Introduce Yourse
 lf" Checkpoint. With any remaining time\, you can discuss any questions yo
 u might have about your grade or the course.\n\n--------------------------
 -----------\nTo Receive Credit for the Checkpoint:\n----------------------
 ---------------\n\nWithin one week of completing your conference appointme
 nt\, return to this page\, click submit assignment\, and answer the questi
 ons below in a text box. Your responses don’t need to be lengthy\, but p
 lease be specific.\n\n* What date and time was your Checkpoint conference
 \, and with whom?\n\n* What feedback can you give about the Checkpoint? Wh
 at did or did not go well? How was it (or could it be more) helpful?\n\n* 
 Give a quick follow-up report about your own participation in the course i
 n general. You set some goals after the first Checkpoint\; how satisfied a
 re you with your performance so far?\n\nRubric: Checkpoint attendance is w
 orth 5 points\, submitted questions 5 points. Late submissions (a missed t
 hen rescheduled appointment or a late report) will receive 25% off.\n\nPol
 icy Reminders\n----------------\n\n* The weekly hours and availability of 
 appointments will be consistent throughout the semester\, and there are mo
 re than enough office hour time slots available to fit in all students ove
 r the length of the semester. However\, it is important that you do not pr
 ocrastinate. We cannot guarantee there will be available appointments late
  in the semester.\n\n* If you cancel fewer than 24 hours before your appoi
 ntment\, are more than 5 minutes late for your time slot\, or do not show 
 up to your appointment\, you may receive reduced or no credit\; contact us
  if there are extenuating circumstances. Missed appointments can be resche
 duled for a late penalty based on availability.\n\n* If you do not schedul
 e a checkpoint\, do not attend a checkpoint\, or plan too late and there a
 re no remaining appointments\, as an alternative\, you can submit a text r
 esponse\, but it will only receive 50% credit. (In response to the checkpo
 int questions above: please state that you did not attend as your answer t
 o question 1. For question 2\, write about the sweet spot(s) you would hav
 e shared in the conference\, in approximately 4–6 sentences. For questio
 n 3\, refer back to the class goals you submitted in the “Introduce Your
 self” checkpoint.)\n\nModule Item Completion (built in browser\, hidden 
 in app)
